 "description": "The first episode of DOOM, from id Software's shareware release 1.9, on\nfbDOOM, a port of the DOOM source code to the Linux framebuffer.\n\nKeys: arrows move and turn, Ctrl fires, Space opens doors, Enter selects\nin the menus, Esc opens the menu, Quit Game ends it, and the logo key\ngoes back to the start menu. Saved games go to the app's folder on the\nSD card. The sound effects play on the output chosen in Settings > Sound;\nthere is no music.\n\nDOOM needs a free block of at least 2 MB of memory for its zone: close\nother apps first if it does not start.",
